    "experience_text": "Use the matched guidance together where supported by the current task and source. If advice conflicts, resolve it against the concrete requirements and explain the choice; do not combine incompatible obligations.\n\nMatched experience 0349feed0bb172ac076a0dc8a0ba1d627e4d8064ed67061453d2e34a35c8ae0e\n0349feed0bb172ac076a0dc8a0ba1d627e4d8064ed67061453d2e34a35c8ae0e:R01 [Applicability]\nObservers share longer-lived cache state, each attempt owns cancellation and completion, signal consumption is recorded on actual access, and paused continuation is deferred.\n\n0349feed0bb172ac076a0dc8a0ba1d627e4d8064ed67061453d2e34a35c8ae0e:R02 [Event relation]\nFor the documented fresh online-mode attempt abandoned entirely offline before entry, prevent reconnect from entering its signal-consuming function with a live signal. Cover both future scheduling and already-queued continuation.\n\n0349feed0bb172ac076a0dc8a0ba1d627e4d8064ed67061453d2e34a35c8ae0e:R03 [Preservation]\nKeep shared consumption bookkeeping separate from attempt resources. Preserve remaining observers, supported unconsumed background completion, cancellation restoration, originating-attempt settlement and stale-completion isolation.\n\n0349feed0bb172ac076a0dc8a0ba1d627e4d8064ed67061453d2e34a35c8ae0e:R04 [Exclusion]\nPaused, observerless or not-yet-entered alone does not establish cancellation policy. Do not invent signal consumption or apply this policy where lazy shared consumption is absent or ownership differs.\n\n0349feed0bb172ac076a0dc8a0ba1d627e4d8064ed67061453d2e34a35c8ae0e:R05 [Verification]\nCheck final-observer departure before and after continuation is queued, reconnect policy variation, cached continuation, later consumption, physical abort/restoration, focus/network modes and retry timing.\n\n\nMatched experience 6cd9c152e8f43aa9b7324cbed5d56edfdd1744d5f497afc0b744c2fc7e8dda2f\n6cd9c152e8f43aa9b7324cbed5d56edfdd1744d5f497afc0b744c2fc7e8dda2f:R01 [Applicability]\nA fresh online-mode query remains offline from mount through unmount, has not entered execution and has lost its final observer.\n\n6cd9c152e8f43aa9b7324cbed5d56edfdd1744d5f497afc0b744c2fc7e8dda2f:R02 [Event relation]\nUnder the current cancellation contract, prevent reconnect from entering that attempt's query function with a still-live cancellation signal. Cover future scheduling and already-queued continuation callbacks.\n\n6cd9c152e8f43aa9b7324cbed5d56edfdd1744d5f497afc0b744c2fc7e8dda2f:R03 [Preservation]\nThis target obligation is independent of refetchOnReconnect. Preserve other legitimate execution, settlement and state restoration.\n\n6cd9c152e8f43aa9b7324cbed5d56edfdd1744d5f497afc0b744c2fc7e8dda2f:R04 [Exclusion]\nNot every paused, unobserved or not-yet-entered query should be canceled. Cached background continuation and different network modes require separate decisions.\n\n6cd9c152e8f43aa9b7324cbed5d56edfdd1744d5f497afc0b744c2fc7e8dda2f:R05 [Verification]\nReconnect after departure, depart after continuation is queued and vary refetchOnReconnect. Check zero entry or entry with an already-canceled signal as the contract permits, rather than only final flags.\n\n\nMatched experience 722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R01 [Applicability]\nThe repair targets panel progress, while queue records, queued notices and public transfer behavior must remain unchanged.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R02 [Event relation]\nKeep records and notices bound to the entry file, attempt, visit and command kind. Display changes must not alter their fields or cardinality.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R03 [Preservation]\nHistorical transfer records are {fileId, attemptId, visitId, kind}. These fields belong to those cases' contracts, not a default API for new systems.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R04 [Exclusion]\nWithout separate authorization, do not add byteCount or infer new business records from file.size. Passing display checks does not establish queue preservation. Automatic Contracts, AST hints and evaluation observations are not new business requirements. Do not modify implementation during analysis or replace the current contract with hidden scores or reference patches.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R05 [Verification]\nCompare record shape, cardinality, queued notices and returned handles across selection, retry, cancellation and navigation reentry.\n\n\nMatched experience e0e19b9f080397cee6acfb1277706af34bc6969547eb0c33a71ca5a0770e64c0\ne0e19b9f080397cee6acfb1277706af34bc6969547eb0c33a71ca5a0770e64c0:R01 [Applicability]\nMultiple observers share work. Canceling consumed work physically terminates it and restores previous query state.\n\ne0e19b9f080397cee6acfb1277706af34bc6969547eb0c33a71ca5a0770e64c0:R02 [Event relation]\nObserver departure changes that observer's lifetime; remaining observers continue sharing. Cancellation settles the originating attempt and restores prior data and status under the contract. Unknown departures remain inert.\n\ne0e19b9f080397cee6acfb1277706af34bc6969547eb0c33a71ca5a0770e64c0:R03 [Preservation]\nPreserve physical abort, prior-state restoration, originating-attempt settlement, later subscription reuse and repeated invalid unsubscription behavior.\n\ne0e19b9f080397cee6acfb1277706af34bc6969547eb0c33a71ca5a0770e64c0:R04 [Exclusion]\nOne departure must not terminate shared work still needed by others. An unknown unsubscription must not be treated as final-observer departure.\n\ne0e19b9f080397cee6acfb1277706af34bc6969547eb0c33a71ca5a0770e64c0:R05 [Verification]\nRemove one observer while another remains, repeat departures and unsubscribe unknown observers, then cancel consumed work and resubscribe. Check shared invocation counts, physical termination and restored data/status.\n\n\nMatched experience 9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R01 [Applicability]\nA source may be reused across visits, attempts or selections of the same file object. Each opening has its own UI lifetime.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R02 [Event relation]\nControl effects with actual visit or attempt identity, not equality of files, channels or transport objects. Later visits obtain their own bootstrap and streaming updates.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R03 [Preservation]\nPreserve shared-source reuse, independent workspaces, subsequent valid uses and existing attempt management.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R04 [Exclusion]\nDo not permanently stop a shared source to suppress old results or let reopening the same object revive a retired visit's publication permission.\n\n9db7de273ed19c3b2c1a15fb54e071117813d3f26ed7a4cb4f4ea2002211a784:R05 [Verification]\nReopen the same object and channel, complete old decoding late and interleave two independent workspaces. Check isolation of old effects and continued operation of the new visit.\n",
